From eb5fa0e702c55c483a82a80094042f34c7fe9645 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Alberto (via Claude)" <alberto8793@icloud.com>
Date: Tue, 16 Jun 2026 03:00:29 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] security(V-10): seal shared/team collaboration artifacts
 before Firestore
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Shared collaboration artifacts were the one CloudVault surface that wrote
source content to Firestore in CLEARTEXT: SharedArtifactCloudCodec.encode
serialized the full file `body`, `title`, and `relativePath` as raw strings
(plus a keyless SHA-256 contentHash confirmation oracle) to
workspaces/workspace-{uid}/.../artifacts/{id} and every versions/{rev} doc,
and firestore.rules permitted it. Anyone with read access to the user's
Firestore namespace (Firebase, a service account, a rules regression, a
subpoena) could read private source content. (Audit: Opus-F-001 — the only
Critical across four independent audits; verified, and absent from every
other parallel remediation plan.)

Fix — bring shared artifacts to parity with chat_threads / conversations /
cli_sessions / session_logs:
- SharedArtifactCloudCodec.encodeSealed seals {title,body,relativePath,
  contentHash} into a single path-bound CloudVault AES-256-GCM envelope
  (AAD = uid|collection|docId|sealedPayload), bound separately for the head
  ("artifacts"+artifactId) and each version ("artifact_versions"+revisionId)
  so an envelope can never be relocated within the vault. Stale cleartext
  fields are FieldValue.delete()'d so a merge write cannot leave plaintext.
- decode opens the envelope when present and falls back to legacy plaintext
  for not-yet-migrated docs (re-sealed on next write).
- CollaborationSyncService resolves the CloudVault key (keyForWriting/Reading,
  mirroring SessionLogSyncService/CLIAgentSessionMirror) and threads it through
  push/commit/pull/decode.
- firestore.rules: sharedArtifactSealedOwnerWrite now REQUIRES contentSealed +
  a path-bound sealedPayload bound to this doc and FORBIDS any cleartext
  content field, for both the head and versions subcollection.

Tests:
- firestore-rules-tests/shared-artifact-sealed.test.js (9 cases, all green in
  the emulator; full suite still passes): plaintext write rejected, sealed
  write accepted, relocation/global-AAD/smuggled-body/missing-envelope
  rejected, head vs version bound distinctly.
- SharedArtifactCloudCodecSealingTests: round-trip, no-cleartext assertion,
  relocation throws, sealed-without-key throws, legacy plaintext still decodes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
